# Assignment 2.2 — Personal Introduction Page

## Objective
To create a resume-style personal introduction webpage using HTML headings, paragraphs, line breaks, horizontal separators, text formatting, and container elements.

## Solution

First, I created a file named `index.html` in Visual Studio Code. I used HTML elements to design a personal introduction webpage similar to a simple resume.

I added my name as the main heading using the `h1` element and created an About Me section with an introduction paragraph using the `p` element. I also created separate sections for education, skills, and hobbies using appropriate headings.

I used heading elements from `h1` to `h6` to organize the content according to its importance. I used the `br` element for line breaks and the `hr` element to separate different sections. I applied `strong` to highlight important information, `em` and `i` to emphasize text, and used `div` elements to group related content. I also used `span` to highlight specific inline text.

Finally, I saved the HTML file and opened it in a web browser to verify that the personal introduction webpage displayed correctly.

## HTML Code

Save the following code as `index.html`.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Personal Introduction</title>
</head>
<body>

    <!-- Main heading -->
    <div>
        <h1>Your Name</h1>
        <p><strong>Student | Aspiring Web Developer</strong></p>
        <p>Email: your-email@example.com</p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <!-- About Me section -->
    <div>
        <h2>About Me</h2>
        <p>
            Hello! My name is <span>Your Name</span>.
            I am a student who is interested in learning
            <em>web development</em> and programming.
            I enjoy learning new technologies and improving my skills.
        </p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <!-- Education section -->
    <div>
        <h2>Education</h2>
        <h3>Current Education</h3>
        <p>
            I am currently pursuing my studies.<br>
            Institution: Your School or College Name<br>
            Qualification: Your Current Qualification
        </p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <!-- Skills section -->
    <div>
        <h2>Skills</h2>
        <h3>Technical Skills</h3>
        <p>
            <strong>HTML</strong> - Basic webpage structure<br>
            <strong>CSS</strong> - Basic webpage styling<br>
            <strong>JavaScript</strong> - Basic interactivity
        </p>

        <h4>Personal Skills</h4>
        <p>Communication, teamwork, and problem-solving.</p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <!-- Hobbies section -->
    <div>
        <h2>Hobbies</h2>
        <p>
            My hobbies include reading books, listening to music,
            learning new skills, and exploring technology.
        </p>
        <p><i>I believe that learning is a continuous process.</i></p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <!-- Career objective section -->
    <div>
        <h2>Career Objective</h2>
        <h5>My Goal</h5>
        <p>
            My goal is to become a skilled web developer and
            create useful and user-friendly websites.
        </p>

        <h6>Personal Motto</h6>
        <p><em>Keep learning and keep growing.</em></p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <div>
        <p>&copy; 2026 Your Name. All rights reserved.</p>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
```

**Note:** Replace `Your Name`, the email address, institution name, and qualification with your own details before submitting.

## Result

The personal introduction webpage was created successfully. It contains a main heading with my name, an About Me section, education details, skills, hobbies, and a career objective. Different HTML elements were used to organize and format the content.

